[{"answer":"So, Michelle, shall we make a start on our presentation?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/1.mp3"},{"answer":"We haven't got that much time left.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/2.mp3"},{"answer":"No, Adam.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/3.mp3"},{"answer":"But at least we've done all the background reading.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/4.mp3"},{"answer":"I found it really interesting.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/5.mp3"},{"answer":"I'd never even heard of the Laki eruption before this.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/6.mp3"},{"answer":"Me neither.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/7.mp3"},{"answer":"I suppose 1783 is a long time ago.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/8.mp3"},{"answer":"But it was a huge eruption","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/9.mp3"},{"answer":"and it had such devastating consequences.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/10.mp3"},{"answer":"I know.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/11-2023-07-01-21-42-02.mp3"},{"answer":"It was great there were so many primary sources to look at.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/12.mp3"},{"answer":"It really gives you a sense of how catastrophic the volcano was.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/13.mp3"},{"answer":"People were really trying to make sense of the science for the first time.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/14.mp3"},{"answer":"That's right.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/15.mp3"},{"answer":"But what I found more significant was how it impacted directly and indirectly on political events,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/16.mp3"},{"answer":"as well as having massive social and economic consequences.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/17.mp3"},{"answer":"I know.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/18.mp3"},{"answer":"That should be the main focus of our presentation.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/19.mp3"},{"answer":"The observations made by people at the time were interesting, weren't they?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/20.mp3"},{"answer":"I mean, they all gave a pretty consistent account of what happened,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/21.mp3"},{"answer":"even if they didn't always use the same terminology.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/22.mp3"},{"answer":"Yeah.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/23.mp3"},{"answer":"I was surprised there were so many weather stations established by that time,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/24.mp3"},{"answer":"so, you know, you can see how the weather changed, often by the hour.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/25.mp3"},{"answer":"Right.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/26.mp3"},{"answer":"Writers at the time talked about the Laki haze to describe the volcanic fog that spread across Europe.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/27.mp3"},{"answer":"They all realised that this wasn't the sort of fog they were used to,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/28.mp3"},{"answer":"and of course this was in pre-industrial times,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/29.mp3"},{"answer":"so they hadn't experienced sulphur-smelling fog before.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/30.mp3"},{"answer":"No, that's true.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/31.mp3"},{"answer":"Reports from the period blamed the haze for an increase in headaches,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/32.mp3"},{"answer":"respiratory issues and asthma attacks.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/33.mp3"},{"answer":"And they all describe how it covered the sun and made it look a strange red colour.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/34.mp3"},{"answer":"Must have been very weird.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/35.mp3"},{"answer":"It's interesting that Benjamin Franklin wrote about the haze.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/36.mp3"},{"answer":"Did you read that?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/37.mp3"},{"answer":"He was the American ambassador in Paris at the time.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/38.mp3"},{"answer":"Yeah.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/39.mp3"},{"answer":"At first no one realised that the haze was caused by the volcanic eruption in Iceland.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/40.mp3"},{"answer":"It was Benjamin Franklin who realised that before anyone else.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/41.mp3"},{"answer":"He's often credited with that, apparently.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/42.mp3"},{"answer":"But a French naturalist beat him to it. I can't remember his name.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/43.mp3"},{"answer":"I'd have to look it up.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/44.mp3"},{"answer":"Then other naturalists had the same idea,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/45.mp3"},{"answer":"all independently of each other.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/46.mp3"},{"answer":"Oh right.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/47.mp3"},{"answer":"We should talk about the immediate impact of the eruption, which was obviously enormous,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/48.mp3"},{"answer":"especially in Iceland, where so many people died.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/49.mp3"},{"answer":"You'd expect that.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/50.mp3"},{"answer":"And the fact that the volcanic ash drifted so swiftly","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/51.mp3"},{"answer":"but not that the effects would go on for so long.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/52.mp3"},{"answer":"Or that two years after the eruption,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/53.mp3"},{"answer":"strange weather events were being reported as far away as North America and North Africa.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/54.mp3"},{"answer":"No.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/55.mp3"},{"answer":"I found all that hard to believe too.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/56.mp3"},{"answer":"It must have been terrible","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/57.mp3"},{"answer":"and there was nothing anyone could do about it,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/58.mp3"},{"answer":"even if they knew the ash cloud was coming in their direction.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/59.mp3"},{"answer":"We should run through some of the terrible consequences of the eruption experienced in different countries.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/60.mp3"},{"answer":"There's quite a varied range.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/61.mp3"},{"answer":"Starting with Iceland, where the impact on farming was devastating.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/62.mp3"},{"answer":"One of the most dramatic things there was the effect on livestock as they grazed in the fields.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/63.mp3"},{"answer":"They were poisoned because they ate vegetation that had been contaminated with fluorine","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/64.mp3"},{"answer":"as a result of the volcanic fallout.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/65.mp3"},{"answer":"That was horrible.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/66.mp3"},{"answer":"In Egypt, the bizarre weather patterns led to a severe drought","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/67.mp3"},{"answer":"and as a result the Nile didn't flood,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/68.mp3"},{"answer":"which meant the crops all failed.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/69.mp3"},{"answer":"It's so far from where the eruption happened","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/70.mp3"},{"answer":"and yet the famine there led to more people dying than any other country.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/71.mp3"},{"answer":"It was worse than the plague.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/72.mp3"},{"answer":"OK.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/73.mp3"},{"answer":"Then in the UK the mortality rate went up a lot, presumably from respiratory illnesses.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/74.mp3"},{"answer":"According to one report it was about double the usual number","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/75.mp3"},{"answer":"and included an unusually high percentage of people under the age of 25.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/76.mp3"},{"answer":"I think people will be surprised to hear that the weather in the USA was badly affected too.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/77.mp3"},{"answer":"George Washington even makes a note in his diary that they were snowbound until March in Virginia.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/78.mp3"},{"answer":"That was before he became president.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/79.mp3"},{"answer":"Yes, and there was ice floating down the Mississippi, which was unprecedented.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/80.mp3"},{"answer":"Astonishing, really.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/81.mp3"},{"answer":"Anyway, what do you think...","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-18-test-2-part-3-2023-06-17-08-35-59/82.mp3"}]
